# What must NOT enter the production image.
#
# The Cloud Build trigger runs `docker build halatuju_api -f halatuju_api/Dockerfile`,
# so THIS file is the one that counts — not `.gcloudignore`, which only applies to
# `gcloud app/functions deploy`. The image is single-stage `COPY . .`, so anything
# not listed here ships to production.
#
# Nothing below is imported by runtime code: checked by grep across every non-test
# module for `apps.*.tests`, `conftest`, and paths into a `tests/` folder.

# Tests and their fixtures (~11 MB) — never imported outside the suite.
apps/*/tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache

# The document-recognition eval corpus (~512 MB of untracked OCR source images, PII).
# The eval scripts and their labels/context JSON STAY: `manage.py eval_doc_recognition`
# defaults to reading them from apps/scholarship/eval.
apps/scholarship/eval/fixtures/

# Build and editor droppings.
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.vscode

# Local-only state and secrets. Production configuration comes from Cloud Run
# environment variables.
.env
.env.*
db.sqlite3

# Prose. No runtime code reads a .md file.
# NOTE: `*` does not cross a `/` in a .dockerignore pattern, so this is the root-level
# prose only (CHANGELOG.md, CLAUDE.md, DEPLOY.md). `docs/` (~230 KB) still ships; widen
# this to `**/*.md` when someone wants it gone, which is safe for the same reason.
*.md
